S = {'cc': 'US', 'fam': 'Capital', 'doc': '# United States 2025: capital income and gains of households (1100), all disposals, stacked on the 1.x model\n\nSources: 26 U.S.C. § 1 (h), § 121, § 1222 (Cornell LII, fetched 2026-11-21; `us/law/`). § 1222: a "short-term capital\ngain" is gain "from the sale or exchange of a capital asset held for not more than 1 year"; long-term above 1 year.\n§ 1 (h) taxes net long-term gains at the preferential rates (the 1.x model\'s `capitalGains`, which holds long-term\ngains); short-term gains are ordinary income: routed into the 1.x model\'s `interest` (taxed at the ordinary rates as\ninterest is: an accounting convention with the same tax). § 121 (b) (1): the gain on a principal residence "shall not\nexceed $250,000" of exclusion ($500,000 on certain joint returns): $250,000 is excluded per main-home sale (upper\nbound for joint filers). Grade B.', 'lean': 'def homeExcl : Int := 250000\ndef gainAfterHome (d : Disposal) : Int := if d.mainHome && d.kind == .home then pos (d.gain - homeExcl) else d.gain\ndef addAll (g : CanonGlobal) : HouseholdAdd :=\n  { routedAdd g with\n    capitalGains := pos (isum ((g.disposals.filter fun d => decide (d.heldMonths > 12)).map gainAfterHome)),\n    interest := (routedAdd g).interest + pos (isum ((g.disposals.filter fun d => decide (d.heldMonths ≤ 12)).map gainAfterHome)) }\ndef capF : Family :=\n  { name := "1100 capital income and gains (all disposals) stacked on the 1.x model", covers := [],\n    run := fun args g _ =>\n      if g.entity == .company then [] else\n      let a := addAll g\n      let tot := a.capitalGains + a.interest + a.dividends + a.rentalIncome\n      if tot == 0 then [] else\n      [charge .pit "Income tax on additional capital income and gains (1.x model, stacked)" tot id\n        (fun _ => stackedTax (pitOf args) g.household a) (event := "capital income") (statute := "26 U.S.C. §§ 1 (h) (long-term rates), 1222 (1 year), 121 (b) ($250,000 home exclusion); 1.x model (stackedTax)")] }\n', 'families': '[capF]', 'unsupported_expr': 'when (g.entity != .company && !g.disposals.isEmpty) "long-term gains at the § 1 (h) rates of the 1.x model (unrecaptured § 1250 gain at 25 % and collectibles at 28 % not separated); short-term gains taxed as ordinary income via the 1.x interest field; long and short results netted separately at zero (no cross-netting, no carry-over); § 121 exclusion $250,000 per main-home sale (ownership and use tests assumed met; $500,000 joint not applied); California taxes gains as ordinary income in the 1.x model"\n  ++ when (g.entity != .company && g.incomes.any fun i => i.kind != .interest && i.kind != .dividend && i.kind != .rent) "additional income items other than interest, dividends and rent: not taxed by this family"', 'guards': ['(addAll { id := "x", household := { id := "x" }, disposals := [{ kind := .realEstate, proceeds := 500, cost := 200, heldMonths := 30 }, { kind := .unlistedShares, proceeds := 300, cost := 100, heldMonths := 6 }] }).capitalGains == 300', '(addAll { id := "x", household := { id := "x" }, disposals := [{ kind := .unlistedShares, proceeds := 300, cost := 100, heldMonths := 6 }] }).interest == 200', 'gainAfterHome { kind := .home, proceeds := 900000, cost := 500000, mainHome := true } == 150000', '(capF.run [] { id := "g", household := { id := "g" } } []).length == 0'], 'taxes': [{'oecd': '1100', 'tax': 'Income tax on additional capital income and gains (all disposals, stacked)', 'statute': '26 U.S.C. §§ 1 (h), 121, 1222; 1.x model', 'dated': 'U.S. Code (Cornell LII) fetched 2026-11-21', 'grade': 'B', 'package': 'P3', 'kernel_parts': ['stackedTax', 'addToRaw'], 'unsupported': ['§ 1250 / collectibles rates', '$500,000 joint exclusion', 'netting and carry-overs']}]}
